        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(openrouter): use dedicated /api/v1/images endpoint for image generation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's OpenRouter image generation currently goes through `/chat/completions`, treating image models as chat models and scraping images out of chat responses with ~300 lines of custom parsing. OpenRouter now ships a dedicated, OpenAI-compatible images endpoint (`POST /api/v1/images`), which is the supported path for image generation going forward and returns images in the standard `data[].b64_json` shape.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe OpenRouter provider is rebuilt on the shared `createOpenAiCompatibleImageGenerationProvider()` factory — the same one used by xAI, DeepInfra, and LiteLLM — so it inherits the common auth, base-URL/config, timeout, SSRF, and response-size handling instead of maintaining a parallel implementation. Two small, backwards-compatible additions to shared code support this:\n\n- A new optional `endpointPath` option on the factory, so a provider can target a flat path like `/api/v1/images` instead of the default `/images/generations` + `/images/edits` split. The path is appended to the resolved base URL; leading and duplicate slashes are normalized (both `\"images\"` and `\"/images\"` resolve to `<baseUrl>/images`), documented on the option and covered by factory tests (string, leading-slash, and per-mode function forms). Providers that don't set it behave exactly as before.\n- The shared OpenAI-compatible response parser now reads `media_type` as a fallback when `mime_type` is absent (OpenRouter labels the image MIME type `media_type`). `mime_type` still wins when present, so other providers are unaffected.\n\nThe request body maps `model`, `prompt`, `n`, plus `aspect_ratio`/`resolution` for Gemini image models and `input_references` (data URLs) for image-to-image. The custom chat-completions parsing (`extractOpenRouterImagesFromResponse` and friends) is deleted.\n\nThe OpenRouter provider also enables the factory's magic-byte MIME sniffing: live testing showed the API omits `media_type` for PNG responses but can also return JPEG bytes without it, so sniffing keeps returned assets correctly labeled (an explicit `media_type` still takes precedence).\n\n## User Impact\n\nOpenRouter image generation and image editing keep working with the same configuration and models, now against OpenRouter's supported dedicated endpoint. Gemini image models gain aspect-ratio and resolution control, and multi-image references are passed through natively. No config changes are required.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Tests\n\n- `pnpm vitest run extensions/openrouter/image-generation-provider.test.ts` — 8 passed\n- `pnpm vitest run src/image-generation/` — 53 passed (includes the shared factory tests, `endpointPath` normalization tests, and a `media_type` fallback test)\n- `pnpm vitest run extensions/{xai,deepinfra,litellm,openai}/image-generation-provider.test.ts` — factory consumers unaffected, all passed\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions:test` and `pnpm tsgo:test:src` — clean (covers the `check-test-types` CI lane)\n- oxlint + oxfmt clean on all changed files\n\n### Live behavior proof (redacted)\n\nRaw endpoint contract — `curl -X POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images` with `{\"model\":\"google/gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview\",\"prompt\":\"a red bicycle leaning against a brick wall\",\"n\":1,\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\"}` (API key redacted). `HTTP 200`; response with `b64_json` elided:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"created\": 0,\n  \"usage\": { \"total_tokens\": 1128 },\n  \"data\": [\n    {\n      \"media_type\": \"(absent — PNG default)\",\n      \"b64_json_len\": 3049104,\n      \"b64_json_prefix\": \"iVBORw0KGgoA\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n(`iVBORw0KGgo` is the base64 of the PNG magic bytes `89 50 4E 47`.)\n\nEnd-to-end through this PR's provider code — a small driver script imports `buildOpenRouterImageGenerationProvider()` from this branch and calls `generateImage()` twice against the live API (text-to-image, then image-to-image feeding the first output back as a reference image):\n\n```text\ntext-to-image  result: model=google/gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview mime=image/jpeg bytes=803555  magic=ffd8ffe0\nimage-to-image result: model=google/gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview mime=image/png  bytes=2020751 magic=89504e47\n```\n\nBoth calls hit `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images` (flat path, no `/images/generations` suffix), decoded to valid images (`file` reports `PNG image data, 1024 x 1024` / JPEG), and the reported `mime` matches the actual magic bytes — including the JPEG case where the API omitted `media_type`, which is what motivated enabling `sniffMimeType`.\n",
        "branch": "openrouter-images-endpoint",
